<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Apr industry output falls 1.3 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Apr industry output falls 1.3 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT  Apr 97     Mar 97	Apr 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -1.3	 +0.3	 +1.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.3	 +3.8	 -1.2</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		99.2	100.5	 97.2</p>
<p>The Economics Ministry warned that the April index was likely to be revised upwards.</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. Previously announced data in parentheses.</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    Apr 97		   Mar 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			77.8	+8.7	71.6	-1.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    97.5	-2.2	99.7	+0.3</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   102.0	-1.4     103.4	-0.6</p>
<p>	Capital goods	97.6	+0.8	96.8	-2.1</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  85.7     -10.7	96.0     +12.1</p>
<p>	Consumer goods     92.5	-5.6	98.0	+1.6</p>
<p> Energy output	    105.9	+3.1     102.7	+2.1</p>
<p> Construction	     115.0	+0.7     114.2	-0.5</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr/Mar 1997 with Feb/Jan 1997:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +0.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  -0.5</p>
<p> Construction			    +7.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -2.0</p>
<p> Mining				    +2.5</p>
<p> Energy output			   unch</p>
<p> Consumer durables and goods	 +1.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    unch</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-Mar 97 with Apr-Mar 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +2.2</p>
<p> Mining				    -2.1</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +3.0</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	   +4.3</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		  +2.1</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	    +6.7</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		 -2.3</p>
<p> Energy output			   -2.4</p>
<p> Construction			    +1.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
